// test-error
// ADR-003 / #1306 review: vendor allocators wrap the same heap.
//
// `heap_caps_malloc` is ESP-IDF's allocator. It used to compile as a bare
// statement while being rejected when its result was assigned -- the same call,
// two answers, because the check was written twice with different matching.
// A name matches when it IS a listed function or ends with `_` and one.
//
// The lookalike controls (`myfree`, `saferealloc`) deliberately live in
// allocator-lookalike-names.test.cnx, NOT here: this fixture's own diagnostic
// halts the analyzer step loop, so a control beside it could never be evaluated
// and could never fail. Mutation-checking caught that -- restoring the old
// substring matching left this fixture green.

void useVendorAllocator() {
    heap_caps_malloc(64);
}
